cff-version: 1.2.0
title: "SuperDARN MSTID Index, North American sector, 2010-2022"
message: "If you use this dataset or software, please cite both this record and Frissell et al. (2016), which defines the index."
type: dataset
authors:
  - family-names: Frissell
    given-names: Nathaniel A.
    orcid: "https://orcid.org/0000-0002-8398-4222"
    affiliation: "Department of Physics and Engineering, The University of Scranton, Scranton, PA, USA"
    email: nathaniel.frissell@scranton.edu
abstract: >-
  Twelve Northern Hemisphere winters (2010-2011 through 2021-2022) of the
  SuperDARN Medium-Scale Traveling Ionospheric Disturbance (MSTID) index,
  computed for ten North American SuperDARN radars at four 2 h daytime
  observational windows per day, together with the script that produces
  climatology and stack plots from it. The index quantifies MSTID-band
  (approximately 14 to 56 min period) fluctuation in a radar's ground-scatter
  field, expressed as a departure from that radar's own seasonal-mean spectrum
  and normalized by the number of contributing ground-scatter cells. It was
  defined by Frissell et al. (2016) and is computed here by the DARNtids
  SuperDARN TID Analysis Toolkit.
keywords:
  - MSTID
  - traveling ionospheric disturbance
  - SuperDARN
  - atmospheric gravity waves
  - polar vortex
  - ionosphere
  - HF radar
